==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[engenious]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{term|ingénieux|lang=frm}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|engenious|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|ingeniosus||endowed with good natural capacity, gifted with genius|lang=la}}, from {{m|la|ingenium||innate or natural quality, natural capacity, genius}}, from {{m|la|in||in}} + {{m|la|gignere||to produce}}, {{etyl|itc-ola|en}} {{m|itc-ola|genere}}. See also [[engine]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-ingenious.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|iːniəs|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Displaying [[genius]] or [[brilliance]]; tending to [[invent]].
#: ''This fellow is '''ingenious'''; he fixed a problem I didn't even know I had.''
# Characterized by [[genius]]; cleverly done or [[contrived]].
#: ''That is an '''ingenious''' model of the atom.''
# [[witty|Witty]]; [[original]]; [[shrewd]]; [[adroit]]; [[keen]]; [[sagacious]].
#: ''He sent me an '''ingenious''' reply for an email.''

====Usage notes====
Do not confuse with [[ingenuous]].

====Synonyms====
* See also [[Wikisaurus:witty]]
* See also [[Wikisaurus:intelligent]]

